Pymtheg patch 0012 (C-21, not upstream): `box` patterns.

Accepts nightly Rust: `box` patterns under `#![feature(box_patterns)]`
(`Err(box E::A { .. })`, `box x @ 1`), as a `box_pattern` node whose child
is the inner pattern. Not stable Rust; real crates built on nightly write it.
`box` is a reserved keyword in every edition, so no valid code binds it.
Reference: https://doc.rust-lang.org/unstable-book/language-features/box-patterns.html
           https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/keywords.html#reserved-keywords
Written independently of upstream's closed pull request "Add box patterns",
https://github.com/tree-sitter/tree-sitter-rust/pull/83 (closed without merge,
2024; same node name), for issue
https://github.com/tree-sitter/tree-sitter-rust/issues/14 (closed).

